cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research or software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "WTI Crude Oil Volatility Research: a benchmarked, reproducible next-week volatility forecaster and a look-ahead-leak post-mortem"
authors:
  - family-names: Bawa
    given-names: Navnoor
version: 2.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NavnoorBawa/WTI-Crude-Oil-Futures"
url: "https://navnoorbawa.github.io/WTI-Crude-Oil-Futures/"
abstract: >-
  Out-of-sample evaluation of next-week realized-volatility forecasts for front-month NYMEX WTI
  crude oil on free data: fourteen models (GARCH family, HAR family, implied volatility, gradient
  boosting, an equal-weight combination) compared with QLIKE, the Model Confidence Set and Hansen's
  SPA test; weekly Value-at-Risk backtests; adaptive conformal intervals; a live forward record that scores
  only forecasts sealed in git before their scoring window opens; and the post-mortem of a retracted
  price-direction model whose backtest was a look-ahead leak. The benchmark evaluation is rebuilt in
  CI from a hash-pinned data snapshot, and the carry and supply-shock studies from committed EIA
  files; the production validation and the post-mortem backtests are committed records of runs on
  downloaded data and are not regenerated in CI.
keywords:
  - realized volatility
  - HAR model
  - implied volatility
  - model confidence set
  - value at risk
  - conformal prediction
  - look-ahead bias
  - crude oil
